      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": "64fba8179addd40969a9bbca",
      "statusChangeNewStatus": "in progress",
      "value": "We're absolutely aware that custom emoji (and other image uploads) on VRChat can be used for these purposes. Reports are good, and we action them, but it does take quite a while to work through reports -- and by that time, the problem has already occured. \n\nWe have been investigating and have already been implementing methods to proactively scan and moderate images uploaded to VRChat. These methods employ services that are also employed on other platforms, much larger than VRChat.\n\nI don't have more info now, but I saw this pop up in my inbox. Wanted to let you know that it is in progress and is nearing deployment. \n\nSince it's a moderation-related system, I can't give much more detail than that, but I'll share what I can when possible!\n\nEdit: Oh, and we've also added in tracked items to consider better ways to see who sent what emoji, or see what emoji a user has access to. Those are probably \"later on\" things because we're confident the scanning systems can solve a majority of these issues first.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
